{"name":"Timberline","hex":"#73573f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"timberline","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The height or limit beyond which trees do not grow in mountainous or Arctic regions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/timberline"}],"entries":[{"title":"Timberline Lodge","blocks":[{"text":"Timberline Lodge is a mountain lodge on the south side of Mount Hood in Clackamas County, Oregon, United States, about 60 miles (97 km) east of Portland. Constructed from 1936 to 1938 by the Works Progress Administration, it was built and furnished by local artisans during the Great Depression. Timberline Lodge was dedicated September 28, 1937, by President Franklin D. Roosevelt."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Timlodge.jpg/330px-Timlodge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timberline_Lodge","wikidata":"Q1574090"},{"title":"Timberline Lodge ski area","blocks":[{"text":"Timberline Lodge ski area is the ski and snowboarding area of Timberline Lodge, a National Historic Landmark in the U.S. state of Oregon. It is one of a few ski areas in the United States with most of the skiable terrain below the main lodge. It is located on the south face of Mount Hood, about 60 miles (95 km) east of Portland, accessible via the Mount Hood Scenic Byway."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Timberline_Lodge_to_Palmer_ski_tour_%288_May_2025%29_%2871645%29.jpg/330px-Timberline_Lodge_to_Palmer_ski_tour_%288_May_2025%29_%2871645%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timberline_Lodge_ski_area","wikidata":"Q7804716"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Snow-Goose-Weather-Vane.jpg/330px-Snow-Goose-Weather-Vane.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Snow-Goose-Weather-Vane.jpg/330px-Snow-Goose-Weather-Vane.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bronze \"snow goose\" weather vane above the head house","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnow-Goose-Weather-Vane.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Timberline-Lodge-Newel-Post.jpg/500px-Timberline-Lodge-Newel-Post.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Timberline-Lodge-Newel-Post.jpg/1280px-Timberline-Lodge-Newel-Post.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Timberline-Lodge-Newel-Post.jpg/500px-Timberline-Lodge-Newel-Post.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATimberline-Lodge-Newel-Post.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Operation_and_Information_WPA_Camp-1936.jpg/500px-Operation_and_Information_WPA_Camp-1936.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Operation_and_Information_WPA_Camp-1936.jpg/1280px-Operation_and_Information_WPA_Camp-1936.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Operation_and_Information_WPA_Camp-1936.jpg/500px-Operation_and_Information_WPA_Camp-1936.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOperation_and_Information_WPA_Camp-1936.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/FDR-Dedicating-Timberline-Lodge-1937.jpg/500px-FDR-Dedicating-Timberline-Lodge-1937.jpg?utm_s